B: I was just nineteen. I had never even seen the sea before I joined the army.
A: What do you remember most about that morning?
B: The noise. The guns never stopped. I was more frightened than I had ever been in my life.
A: How did you reach the beach?
B: Our boat was hit, so we had to swim the last part. Many of my friends never made it to the sand.
A: Do you still think about them?
B: Every single day. That is why I come back here each year, to remember the ones we lost.', '记者采访一位登陆日老兵布朗先生。他说自己当年才十九岁,参军前从没见过海。那天清晨他记得最深的是枪炮声不停,他从未那么害怕过。他们的船被击中,只能游完最后一段,许多战友再也没能上岸。他每年都回来,为的是纪念逝去的战友。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How old was Mr Brown on the day of the landings?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Nineteen.","Fifteen.","Twenty-five.","Thirty."]},{"q":"What did he remember most about that morning?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The cold rain.","The endless noise of the guns.","The taste of the food.","The long train ride."]},{"q":"Why did the men have to swim the last part?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Their boat had been hit.","They wanted to train harder.","The bridge was broken.","The water was warm and calm."]},{"q":"What happened to many of his friends?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They went home early.","They died before reaching the beach.","They became officers.","They were taken prisoner."]},{"q":"Why does Mr Brown return every year?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To meet famous film stars.","To sell his old uniform.","To remember the friends he lost.","To look for a new job."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U3', 'fltrp');
B: Not really. There are so many. I was thinking of one about the D-Day landings.
A: That sounds good. I might read the story of a wartime university instead, the one that moved thousands of kilometres on foot.
B: Oh, Lianda? My grandfather told me about that. The students kept studying even while bombs were falling.
A: Exactly. I find that more moving than the battles. It shows a different side of war.
B: Then we''ll have two different reviews. Shall we share our books when we finish?
A: Good idea. We can learn about both the fighting and the spirit behind it.', '两名学生在选老师布置的战争主题读物并写书评。男生还没定,想读关于诺曼底登陆的书。女生想读那所徒步迁移数千公里的战时大学(联大)的故事,因为学生们在炸弹落下时仍坚持学习,她觉得这比战役更动人。两人决定各写不同的书评,读完后互相交换书,既了解战斗,也了解背后的精神。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the teacher want each student to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Read a war book and write a review.","Watch a film in class.","Draw a map of Europe.","Interview a real soldier."]},{"q":"Which topic is the boy thinking of reading about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A peace garden.","The D-Day landings.","A modern factory.","A football match."]},{"q":"What will the girl read about?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The building of new ships.","A trip to the seaside.","A wartime university that moved on foot.","The life of a film star."]},{"q":"Why does she find that story moving?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The school was very rich.","The students never had any classes.","The war never reached the school.","Students kept studying even under bombing."]},{"q":"What do the two students agree to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Share their books when they finish.","Write a single review together.","Give up the task.","Ask for an easier book."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U3', 'fltrp');
B: That''s a fair question. What do you think we might gain from it?
A: I suppose we learn some dates and names.
B: More than that. When we understand how much war cost ordinary people, we work harder to keep the peace.
A: So it''s a kind of warning?
B: Yes. The people who lived through it are growing fewer every year. If we forget their stories, we may one day repeat their mistakes.
A: I never thought of it that way. I''ll read my book more carefully now.
B: Good. Remembering is the first step towards peace.', '学生问老师为什么要学这么多久远的战争。老师反问能从中得到什么。学生以为只是记些日期和人名。老师说不止如此:当我们明白战争给普通人带来多大代价,就会更努力地维护和平。学生问这是不是一种警示。老师说是的,经历过战争的人一年比一年少,若忘了他们的故事,有朝一日可能重蹈覆辙。学生表示要更认真地读书,老师说铭记是走向和平的第一步。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the student ask the teacher?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["When the test will be held.","Where the war took place.","Why they must study old wars.","How to write a poem."]},{"q":"What does the student first think they learn?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["How to fight a battle.","How to draw maps.","How to make weapons.","Some dates and names."]},{"q":"According to the teacher, what makes people value peace?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Understanding war''s cost to ordinary people.","Winning more battles.","Building bigger armies.","Forgetting the past quickly."]},{"q":"Why is it urgent to record the stories now?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The books are being lost.","The people who lived through war are fewer each year.","Wars never happen any more.","Young people refuse to listen."]},{"q":"What does the teacher say is the first step towards peace?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Forgetting.","Fighting.","Remembering.","Travelling."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U3', 'fltrp');

